<%# The backlog tree: every epic in the project, its stories under it, its tasks
    under those. §7's key screen, and the only one that shows containment whole
    — everywhere else in the app reaching a task takes five navigations and you
    can never see two epics at once.

    Epics open and stories closed is the default on purpose. Open, the tree
    answers "what is the state of this project" at the altitude people actually
    ask it: every epic and every story at once. Tasks are the detail behind one
    story, and expanding them all would bury the shape of the thing. %>
<ul class="mt-4 space-y-2">
  <% epics.each do |epic| %>
    <%= render layout: "backlog/branch",
          locals: { project: project, record: epic, children: epic.stories,
                    child_label: "Stories", progress: epic.progress, expanded: true } do %>
      <% epic.stories.each do |story| %>
        <%= render layout: "backlog/branch",
              locals: { project: project, record: story, children: story.tasks,
                        child_label: "Tasks", progress: story.progress, expanded: false } do %>
          <% story.tasks.each do |task| %>
            <%= render "backlog/branch",
                  project: project, record: task, children: [],
                  child_label: "Tasks", progress: nil, expanded: false %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
</ul>
